    "diff_hunk": "@@ -174,7 +174,9 @@ By including the lower timestamp bits in the trace encapsulation, each trace pac\n \n For Smstrcn1p0/Ssstrcn1p0, timestamping follows the method described in section 8.5 of RISC-V N-Trace (Nexus-based Trace) v1.0 Specification.  As described for E-trace above, all N-trace packets can be associated with a precise timestamp value.\n \n-WARNING: _We should have a timestamp width recommendation here._\n+Some implementations may opt to include only a subset of the `time` CSR value when the full trace timestamp is reported, to reduce both trace packet size and the hardware required to support it.  It is recommended that implementations include enough lower bits of `time` to ensure the timer does not wrap for at least 24 hours.",
